{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -fsSL https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/llms.txt; command -v qrypt-run; node --version; python3 --version; grep -q '\"'^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED]\"' .env && echo set\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl -fsSL https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/llms.txt; command -v qrypt-run; node --version; python3 --version; grep -q '\"'^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED]\"' .env && echo set\"","aggregated_output":"# Qrypt quantum entropy quickstart (for AI agents)\n> Get an AES-256-GCM key from Qrypt quantum entropy. Plain HTTPS; no SDK exists for this API. Do not invent one.\n\n## FIRST: secrets and layout\n- If .env exists, it already has the token. Do NOT read or print it in any form (no cat/head/sed/less, not even masked). Only check: grep -q '^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] .env && echo set\n- Write all files in the current directory next to .env. No subfolder, no copying .env.\n- Keep the generated key in memory only. Do NOT write it to a file (no aes-256.key, no key.bin), print it or log it. \"Generate a key\" means: run the AES-GCM round trip and print the success line. Long-term key storage belongs in a secret manager or KMS and is out of scope here.\n- If .env gives \"Permission denied\", you are in the Qrypt agent sandbox ON PURPOSE. Do not try to read it or work around it. Run your program with: qrypt-run quickstart.py (or qrypt-run quickstart.mjs). Only qrypt-run can read .env.\n- Humans: to keep agents from reading .env, run the agent in the sandbox: see \"Using an AI coding agent?\" on the quickstart page (files at /agent-sandbox/).\n\n## API\nGET https://api-eus.qrypt.com/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1\nHeaders: Authorization: Bearer $QRYPT_API_KEY ; Accept: application/json\nResponse: {\"random\": [\"<base64>\"], \"size\": 1}. Each string decodes (standard base64) to 1024 bytes.\nsize counts KiB (1..512), NOT bytes. For one AES-256 key use size=1 and take the first 32 decoded bytes.\n\n## Rules\n- Python: use `requests` or set a custom User-Agent. Cloudflare blocks Python-urllib with 403 Error 1010.\n- Read the token from .env (QRYPT_API_KEY). Never print, log or commit the token or key.\n- Never show .env or any part of it (no `cat .env`, no `head -c N .env`). To check it is set: `grep -q '^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] .env && echo set`\n- Build the project in the directory that already holds .env. Do not copy .env into a new subfolder.\n- 400 bad size; 401 missing/malformed Authorization header; 403 wrong token OR quota reached (bad tokens return 403, not 401);\n  429 rate limited (docs: 30 req/10 s, but live can return 429 about 1 s after a single prior call; no Retry-After): wait 10 s or more and never loop; 500/503 try again shortly. Exit non-zero on error.\n\n## Python (isolated install: python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv; run with .venv/bin/python)\n# Qrypt quickstart (Python): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -> AES-256-GCM key.\n# Setup: pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv\n# Then put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token> in a .env file next to this script.\nimport base64\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport requests\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead import AESGCM\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nAPI = os.getenv(\"QRYPT_BASE_URL\", \"https://api-eus.qrypt.com\")  # mock override\n\n# One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.\nHELP = {None: \"QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env (see .env.example).\",\n        400: \"400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.\",\n        401: \"401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.\",\n        403: \"403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.\",\n        429: \"429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single \"\n             \"prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.\"}\n# 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.\n\n# Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.\nload_dotenv()\ntoken = os.getenv(\"QRYPT_API_KEY\") or sys.exit(HELP[None])\n\n# Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy. A custom User-Agent avoids Cloudflare's\n# block on Python's urllib; X-Qrypt-Client tags quickstart traffic.\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\",\n    \"User-Agent\": \"qrypt-quickstart/1.0\", \"X-Qrypt-Client\": \"quickstart-py/1.0\"}\ntry:\n    resp = requests.get(f\"{API}/api/v1/quantum-entropy\", params={\"size\": 1},\n                        headers=headers, timeout=15)\n    if resp.status_code != 200:\n        sys.exit(HELP.get(resp.status_code, f\"{resp.status_code}: Qrypt is \"\n                          \"busy or erroring. Try again shortly.\"))\n    entropy_b64 = resp.json()[\"random\"][0]\nexcept (requests.RequestException, ValueError):\n    sys.exit(\"Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.\")\n\n# Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.\nkey = base64.b64decode(entropy_b64)[:32]\n\n# Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.\naes, nonce, message = AESGCM(key), os.urandom(12), b\"hello, quantum entropy\"\nassert aes.decrypt(nonce, aes.encrypt(nonce, message, None), None) == message\nprint(\"Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).\")\n\n## Node 20.12+ (no deps)\n// Qrypt quickstart (Node 20.12+): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -> AES-256-GCM key.\n// No dependencies. Put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token> in a .env file here.\nimport assert from \"node:assert\";\nimport { existsSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { createCipheriv, createDecipheriv, randomBytes } from \"node:crypto\";\n\nconst API = process.env.QRYPT_BASE_URL ?? \"https://api-eus.qrypt.com\"; // mock\n\n// One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.\nconst HELP = { missing: \"QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env.\",\n  network: \"Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.\",\n  400: \"400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.\",\n  401: \"401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.\",\n  403: \"403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.\",\n  429: \"429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single \" +\n    \"prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.\" };\n// 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.\nconst fail = (msg) => { console.error(msg); process.exit(1); };\n\n// Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.\nif (existsSync(\".env\")) process.loadEnvFile(\".env\");\nconst token = process.env.QRYPT_API_KEY || fail(HELP.missing);\n\n// Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy (size counts KiB, not bytes).\nconst headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, Accept: \"application/json\",\n  \"User-Agent\": \"qrypt-quickstart/1.0\", \"X-Qrypt-Client\": \"quickstart-js/1.0\" };\nconst url = `${API}/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1`;\nconst res = await fetch(url, { headers }).catch(() => fail(HELP.network));\nif (res.status !== 200) fail(HELP[res.status] ??\n  `${res.status}: Qrypt is busy or erroring. Try again shortly.`);\nconst body = await res.json().catch(() => fail(HELP.network));\n\n// Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.\nconst key = Buffer.from(body.random[0], \"base64\").subarray(0, 32);\n\n// Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.\nconst GCM = \"aes-256-gcm\", iv = randomBytes(12), message = \"hello, quantum\";\nconst enc = createCipheriv(GCM, key, iv);\nconst sealed = Buffer.concat([enc.update(message, \"utf8\"), enc.final()]);\nconst dec = createDecipheriv(GCM, key, iv).setAuthTag(enc.getAuthTag());\nassert.equal(dec.update(sealed, null, \"utf8\") + dec.final(\"utf8\"), message);\nconsole.log(\"Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).\");\n\n## More\nTroubleshooting: /troubleshooting\n/usr/local/bin/qrypt-run\nv24.22.0\nPython 3.11.2\ngrep: .env: Permission denied\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
